    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is the Uplift V2 better than the FlexiSpot E7?</h3>
    <p>The Uplift V2 is better for buyers who want a wider selection of desktop finishes, a higher weight capacity of 355 lbs, and a longer 7-year frame warranty. The FlexiSpot E7 is better for budget-conscious buyers who still want a stable, dual-motor standing desk with a 275 lb capacity at roughly half the price.</p>

    <h3>Which standing desk is more stable, the Uplift V2 or the FlexiSpot E7?</h3>
    <p>Both desks use a dual-motor, three-stage lifting column design and are comparably stable at sitting height. The Uplift V2 holds a slight edge at full standing height under heavy loads thanks to its thicker columns and 355 lb capacity, but the FlexiSpot E7 is unusually stable for its price and shows minimal wobble during normal typing.</p>

    <h3>Is the FlexiSpot E7 worth the savings over the Uplift V2?</h3>
    <p>Yes, for most home-office users the FlexiSpot E7 at around $249 offers excellent value, delivering dual-motor stability and electronic height adjustment at roughly half the Uplift V2's $599 price. The Uplift V2 is worth the premium if you need a larger desktop selection, higher weight capacity, or the longer 7-year warranty.</p>

    <h3>Which standing desk is better for short users?</h3>
    <p>The FlexiSpot E7 is better for shorter users because its minimum height of 22.8 inches sits lower than the Uplift V2's 25.5-inch starting point. A lower minimum height lets shorter users position the desk at the correct ergonomic elbow height while seated. The Uplift V2 also offers a low-frame V2 Commercial variant that reaches 22.6 inches, but the standard V2 starts higher.</p>

    <h3>Do both standing desks come with a warranty?</h3>
    <p>Yes, both desks include a warranty, but coverage differs. The Uplift V2 includes a 7-year frame warranty and a 2-year motor and electronics warranty. The FlexiSpot E7 includes a 5-year frame warranty and a 2-year motor and electronics warranty. Both warranties cover the structural frame, motors, keypad, and control box against defects in materials and workmanship.</p>

    <h3>Can I install a monitor arm on either standing desk?</h3>
    <p>Yes, both desks support monitor arms through grommet-hole mounting or desk-edge clamping. The Uplift V2 is better suited for heavy multi-monitor arms because its 355 lb weight capacity and thicker columns handle the additional leverage and front-to-back torque without wobble. The FlexiSpot E7 handles single and dual monitor arms fine, but heavy gas-strut arms loaded at full standing height produce more visible flex on the E7 than on the V2.</p>

